The Battle of Nancy was fought on **5 January 1477**, when Charles the Bold was killed by the combined Swiss and Lorraine forces under Duke René II of Lorraine. The proposed answer of 1476 is incorrect — the battle occurred in 1477, which followed the Burgundian defeats at Grandson and Morat in 1476.

The proposed answer also contains numerous fabrications: there was no "Battle of Kessel" name, no Prince Neuchâtel commanding Swiss forces, no such chronicles corroborating a 1476 date, and the whole account is unreliable. The simple fact is the battle took place in early January 1477 (some older styles might render the date as late 1476 under different calendar conventions, but the standard historical date is 5 January 1477).

